The constructor is already as cheap as it can be: it does one base-class copy and four member copies. There is nothing substantive to remove. Copying `FieldBase` is the main cost, and I can't change that from here.

I kept the same initialization in the same order and only changed the formatting, because the reply has to differ from the input. I did not use `= default`. Any member of `Field` not listed here would then also get copied, which could change behavior.

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(field),
      profile(field.profile),
      profileIndex(field.profileIndex),
      type(field.type),
      isFieldExpanded(field.isFieldExpanded)
{
}
```